 {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Herbert+Leave+Me+Now", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/551340736", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Herbert+Leave+Me+Now", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Herbert+Leave+Me+Now&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2000 Accidental Records Ltd"]}, {"t": 6840, "time": "01:54:00", "artist": "Bakermat & RANI", "title": "I Love Life (feat. RANI)", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Bakermat+%26+RANI+I+Love+Life+%28feat.+RANI%29", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bakermat+%26+RANI+I+Love+Life+%28feat.+RANI%29", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Bakermat+%26+RANI+I+Love+Life+%28feat.+RANI%29", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Bakermat+%26+RANI+I+Love+Life+%28feat.+RANI%29", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1889524495", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Bakermat+%26+RANI+I+Love+Life+%28feat.+RANI%29", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Bakermat+%26+RANI+I+Love+Life+%28feat.+RANI%29&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2026 Big Top Amsterdam"]}], "counts": {"high": 6, "mid": 11, "low": 11}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:01:38", "end": "00:02:44", "text": "A very good evening and welcome to Monday Sunset. My name's Simon Caldwell. I'm with you for the next couple of hours flying solo as Maddie and James are out of the state. Got a bunch of new music to play for you, including a fair few of these set of down-tempo house tracks, especially to start us off. I hope you can dig. You can stream along at FBi.radio. And if you'd like to get in touch You can text in on 0435 123 945 Can't promise a live playlist tonight But we'll get one"}, {"start": "00:06:37", "end": "00:07:03", "text": ""}, {"start": "00:26:14", "end": "00:27:03", "text": "Due to FBi Radio 94.5, this is Monday Sunset, rolling through some tracks, most of them new, brand new. This one is a track by Ali Berger on the label Scissor and Thread, which is a really interesting label out of Brooklyn, New York. Before this one was a brand new one by Charisma called Open Your Eyes. before that was another one from scissor and thread was by fka borson called from space between and starting up the program was frank and tony with dj sprinkles from this very same label that's a new one called companion"}, {"start": "00:27:15", "end": "00:27:32", "text": "Francis and Rupert the Dog in Campertown. Also great to have the Professor and Tanya on board and great to hear from you also, Scott, in Queenseye. If you want to get in touch, it's 0435 123 945."}, {"start": "00:45:33", "end": "00:46:28", "text": "Tune to FBi 94.5, this Monday's Sunset. This is a brand new one, I think a little forthcoming actually, by John DeHarda, extremely prolific producer from LA. This one's called The Hidden Face and I believe it's on his own label, Palette Recordings. Before this, something from a year or two ago, that was Abacus who's from Toronto. He's been making lovely deep house music since the early 90s. that one was called Mortise and Tenon that's out on Kai Alce's label MDATL and before that was King Crowny with Zoe Kipri on vocals remixed by Wes Wint"}, {"start": "01:20:21", "end": "01:21:49", "text": "You're tuned to FBi Radio 94.5. It's Monday Sunset with me, Simon Rowling, solo this week. And on a fairly chill tip, I think you'll probably agree, this is a track by Brunson called My Friend Ryan for this one from that great label Scissor and Thread that I've somehow missed out on until recently. That was a track by Frank and Tony with DJ Archmael called Drift. Before that, a new release by Stephen Brown, a Scottish producer who's been around since the 90s but has an active band camp now. That track was called Tell Him. Before that, the great Fred P with a track called LG Fantasy. And before that was another old-timer, but a not-so-old track. That was Claude Young Jr. from Detroit. One of the more incredible DJs back in the day. That was a track called Santa Barbara, released on Kyle C's label. And we also heard another Detroit artist, Terrence Parker, praise Melody Break. And a big shout-out to Matt. and also to Stav glad the selection is calming you down it's kind of the point and also a big shout out to Mr. H"}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:00:00"}, "track": {"title": "On My Side", "artists": [{"name": "darlynn"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:03:00"}, "track": {"title": "Companion With DJ Sprinkles (Original Mix)", "artists": [{"name": "Frank & Tony"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:12:00"}, "track": {"title": "From Space Between (Frank & Tony's Housebeat Dub)", "artists": [{"name": "fka boursin"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:18:00"}, "track": {"title": "The Harp (feat. LaRae Starr) [Beckwith Extended Remix]", "artists": [{"name": "Dantiez Saunderson"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:19:47"}, "track": {"title": "Open Your Eyes", "artists": [{"name": "Soul In The Horn & Karizma"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:25:00"}, "track": {"title": "0221 (Serious Mix)", "artists": [{"name": "Ali Berger"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:32:32"}, "track": {"title": "Coat On", "artists": [{"name": "KingCrowney & ZOE Kypri"}]}, "isPremiere"